    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 202,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 203,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 58,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 59,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: To find the maximum value of \\( ab^2 c^3 d^4 \\) given the constraint \\( a + b + c + d = 10 \\), we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers or apply the AM-GM inequality directly for simplicity."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 376,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 378,
        "char_start": 205,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 139,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 140,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Apply the AM-GM inequality to the terms \\( a, \\frac{b}{2}, \\frac{b}{2}, \\frac{c}{3}, \\frac{c}{3}, \\frac{c}{3}, \\frac{d}{4}, \\frac{d}{4}, \\frac{d}{4}, \\frac{d}{4} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 677,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 678,
        "char_start": 380,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 289,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 290,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: According to AM-GM, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{a + \\frac{b}{2} + \\frac{b}{2} + \\frac{c}{3} + \\frac{c}{3} + \\frac{c}{3} + \\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{4}}{10} \\geq \\sqrt[10]{a \\cdot \\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{c}{3}\\right)^3 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{d}{4}\\right)^4}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 779,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 780,
        "char_start": 680,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 334,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 335,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Simplify the left side of the inequality:\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b + c + d}{10} = \\frac{10}{10} = 1\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 932,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 933,
        "char_start": 782,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 401,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 402,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Therefore, we get:\n\\[\n1 \\geq \\sqrt[10]{a \\cdot \\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{c}{3}\\right)^3 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{d}{4}\\right)^4}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1119,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1120,
        "char_start": 935,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 476,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 477,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Raise both sides to the power of 10 to eliminate the root:\n\\[\n1^{10} \\geq a \\cdot \\left(\\frac{b}{2}\\right)^2 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{c}{3}\\right)^3 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{d}{4}\\right)^4\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1226,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1227,
        "char_start": 1122,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 530,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 531,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: This simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 \\geq a \\cdot \\frac{b^2}{4} \\cdot \\frac{c^3}{27} \\cdot \\frac{d^4}{256}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1350,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1351,
        "char_start": 1229,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 590,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 591,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Multiply both sides by \\( 4 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 256 \\):\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 256 \\geq a \\cdot b^2 \\cdot c^3 \\cdot d^4\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1434,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1435,
        "char_start": 1353,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 626,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 627,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Calculate the product on the left side:\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 256 = 27648\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1489,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1490,
        "char_start": 1437,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 658,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 659,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Thus, we have:\n\\[\n27648 \\geq ab^2 c^3 d^4\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1613,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1615,
        "char_start": 1492,
        "effective_step": 11,
        "end_token_index": 708,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 709,
        "step_number": 11,
        "text": "Step 11: The equality in AM-GM holds when all the terms are equal, i.e., \\( a = \\frac{b}{2} = \\frac{c}{3} = \\frac{d}{4} \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1726,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1728,
        "char_start": 1617,
        "effective_step": 12,
        "end_token_index": 771,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 772,
        "step_number": 12,
        "text": "Step 12: Let \\( a = k, \\frac{b}{2} = k, \\frac{c}{3} = k, \\frac{d}{4} = k \\). Then \\( b = 2k, c = 3k, d = 4k \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1834,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1835,
        "char_start": 1730,
        "effective_step": 13,
        "end_token_index": 826,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 827,
        "step_number": 13,
        "text": "Step 13: Substitute these into the sum constraint:\n\\[\nk + 2k + 3k + 4k = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10k = 10\n\\]\n\\[\nk = 1\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1881,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1883,
        "char_start": 1837,
        "effective_step": 14,
        "end_token_index": 855,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 856,
        "step_number": 14,
        "text": "Step 14: So, \\( a = 1, b = 2, c = 3, d = 4 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2023,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2024,
        "char_start": 1885,
        "effective_step": 15,
        "end_token_index": 926,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 927,
        "step_number": 15,
        "text": "Step 15: Substitute these values back into \\( ab^2 c^3 d^4 \\):\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 2^2 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 4^4 = 1 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 256 = 27648\n\\]"
      }
    ]
